    <div class="bg-sky-50 border-l-4 border-sky-500 p-6 mb-10 rounded-r-xl">
      <p class="font-semibold text-sky-900 mb-2">Quick answer</p>
      <p class="text-sky-900">
        A Canada visitor visa (temporary resident visa, or TRV) applied for from outside Canada currently takes anywhere from about two weeks to more than three months, depending on the country you apply from. IRCC's figures, last updated November 4, 2026, show 32 days for India, 24 days for the Philippines, 51 days for China, 58 days for Pakistan and 103 days for Nigeria. The figure includes biometrics and reflects how long IRCC took to finish 80% of recent applications. The fee is $100 per person plus $85 for biometrics.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
